WEBVTT

00:44:27.430 --> 00:44:32.350
but to try to show the enthusiasm
in a way that will feel real to him.

00:44:32.374 --> 00:44:34.278
CA: Right, will actually break through.

00:44:34.302 --> 00:44:37.518
He won't go, "Oh, clearly she doesn't
think that matters that much."

00:44:37.542 --> 00:44:38.695
SC: Yeah! Exactly.

00:44:38.719 --> 00:44:42.674
And that's an insight that you need
to have not only one time,

00:44:42.698 --> 00:44:46.682
but it's like I have to have it every day,
I have to remind myself about that.

00:44:46.706 --> 00:44:49.409
And I see that happening
not only in marriages,

00:44:49.433 --> 00:44:51.152
but in workplaces, too.

00:44:51.176 --> 00:44:54.861
I'll often hear from people who will think
that their introverted colleagues

00:44:54.885 --> 00:44:57.438
don't care about something
that just happened,

00:44:57.462 --> 00:44:59.325
great for the team or something,

00:44:59.349 --> 00:45:02.681
and then you talk to that person
and they actually care really deeply.